# Versioned CMake library outputs must bind Conan library metadata to the physical linker file.
id:                     E2184-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|CMakeDeps|conan-create
phase:                  package|consumer-validation
error_signature:        "Library '.*' not found in package|CMakeDeps.*library.*not found in package"
severity:               2
category:               conan|cmake|package_info|metadata
match_keywords:         versioned shared library output, CMakeDeps library not found, cpp_info.libs, physical linker basename, package consumer
root_cause:             CMake projects may add an ABI version to the installed shared-library filename (for example libtbb.so.12.3 or libtbb12.dll.a) while retaining an unversioned namelink or logical target name (libtbb.so and TBB::tbb). Declaring one platform's linker lookup name for every target makes CMakeDeps search for a file that is not present, so the package builds but its consumer configuration fails.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for CMake libraries whose install tree uses versioned shared-library or import-library basenames.
verification_cmd:       Build and package the recipe, list package lib/ contents, then run conan create with a real consumer; require CMakeDeps configure and the consumer executable to pass.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           physical-library-metadata-binding
rec_description:        After package(), derive cpp_info.libs from the platform's actual linker lookup name while preserving the upstream CMake target name in set_property(cmake_target_name). Verify the Windows import-library layout separately from the OHOS/Linux shared-library namelink layout, and branch on shared/static mode when names differ.
rec_command:            "conan create <recipe> -c tools.build:jobs=2; inspect package lib/; run test_package consumer"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      package-tree-readback
fallback_description:   If naming differs by platform, read the package tree in package_info context and bind per-platform names explicitly; do not add fake symlinks or claim a consumer pass from the producer build alone.
fallback_command:       "read package lib/ and platform CMake target import locations; update cpp_info.libs and rerun consumer"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          consumer-validation
forbid_1_pattern:       "cpp_info.libs.*logical target name.*without.*physical"
forbid_1_reason:        CMakeDeps resolves library files from cpp_info.libs and cannot infer a versioned physical basename.
forbid_1_consequence:   The producer may package successfully while every downstream CMake configure fails.
forbid_2_pattern:       "consumer.*skip|producer.*pass.*consumer"
forbid_2_reason:        Producer compilation does not validate generated consumer metadata.
forbid_2_consequence:   A broken package can reach CI or a downstream task undetected.
principles:             P007, P015
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
